// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ⚠️ VERY IMPORTANT ABOUT CHARACTER NAMES
// ------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Write the character name that the AI is most likely to use
// when referring to that character.
//
// Ideally, this should match one of the character's Story Card
// triggers.
//
// Example:
//
//     characters: {
//       "Mira": 60
//     }
//
// is preferable to:
//
//     characters: {
//       "Mira the Innkeeper": 60
//     }
//
// if the AI normally calls her simply "Mira".
//
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ⚠️ VERY IMPORTANT ABOUT ALIASES
// ------------------------------------------------------------
//
// The main "name" of the location is AUTOMATICALLY treated as
// one of its triggers.
//
// You only need to put additional ways of referring to the
// same place inside "aliases".
//
// Example:
//
//     name: "Old Harbor"
//
//     aliases: [
//       "the Old Harbor",
//       "Old Harbor docks",
//       "the harbor",
//       "the docks"
//     ]
//
// This makes the system recognize all of those as the SAME
// location.
//
// Try to use aliases that are distinctive enough that they
// will not accidentally match unrelated text.
//
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// 🎲 ABOUT LOCATION PROBABILITY
// ------------------------------------------------------------
//
// There are TWO location probabilities:
//
//     firstEntryChance
//
//         Chance that the system will attempt an NPC spawn
//         when the player enters the location for the first time.
//
//     revisitChance
//
//         Chance that the system will attempt an NPC spawn
//         when the player returns to the location later.
//
// Both values are literal percentages:
//
//     0   = 0%
//     25  = 25%
//     50  = 50%
//     100 = 100%
//
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// 🎲 ABOUT CHARACTER PROBABILITY
// ------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Character numbers are RELATIVE WEIGHTS.
//
// They determine who is selected if the location spawn
// actually happens.
//
// Example:
//
//     characters: {
//       "Mira": 60,
//       "Bram": 30,
//       "Nell": 10
//     }
//
// You can think of that as:
//
//     Mira  = 60
//     Bram  = 30
//     Nell  = 10
//
// So Mira is twice as likely as Bram, and Bram is three times
// as likely as Nell.
//
// The numbers do NOT have to add up to 100.
//
// These are equivalent:
//
//     60 / 30 / 10
//
//     6 / 3 / 1
//
//     600 / 300 / 100
//
// If making the numbers add up to 100 feels easier, do it.
// That is perfectly fine.
//
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// 👥 ABOUT charactersPerSpawn
// ------------------------------------------------------------
//
// This determines how many DIFFERENT characters the spawn
// event can select.
//
//     1 = one character
//     2 = two characters
//     3 = three characters
//
// For most locations, 1 is recommended.
//
// If you set this to 2, the engine selects two different
// characters according to their weights.
//
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ✏️ QUICK EXAMPLE
// ------------------------------------------------------------
//
//     firstEntryChance: 40,
//     revisitChance: 15,
//
//     charactersPerSpawn: 1,
//
//     characters: {
//       "Mira": 60,
//       "Bram": 30,
//       "Nell": 10
//     }
//
// Means:
//
//   → First time in the location: 40% chance of a spawn.
//   → Returning later: 15% chance of a spawn.
//   → One character will be selected.
//   → Mira is the most likely.
//   → Bram is half as likely as Mira.
//   → Nell is the least likely.
//
// ============================================================


